<speak>I recommend reducing your holding in Orion Global Income Fund because that releases cash for your expenses and reduces your remaining exposure to interest-rate and credit fluctuations. For Orion Global Income Fund, rising interest rates can lower the value of the bonds it holds and bring down its unit value. A limit sale may also remain unexecuted if the dealing price does not meet your limit. The transaction charge for this sale is 0.3%.</speak>